      <div class="rd-inner">
        <div class="rd-eyebrow">Coaching &amp; Supervision</div>
        <h1 class="rd-h2">Frequently asked questions</h1>
        <div class="rd-faq-grid">
          <div class="rd-faq-list">
            <div class="rd-faq-item is-active">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="true"><span class="rd-num">01</span><span class="rd-q">How do coaching, supervision and therapy differ?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Coaching focuses on professional or personal goals, decisions and roles, for example stepping into a leadership role, changing careers, questions about parenting, or dealing with stressful relationship situations.</p><p>Supervision looks at your professional practice: your work with clients, collaboration within the team and the structures of your organization. Therapy and counseling are the right fit when you want to go deeper, or where complex relationship difficulties, emotional distress or crises are at the forefront.</p><p>The boundaries are fluid. In our first session, we work out together which setting fits your concern.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">02</span><span class="rd-q">What concerns can I bring to coaching?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><ul class="rd-faq-ul"><li><strong>Role and leadership:</strong> stepping into a leadership role or changes in your role</li><li><strong>Direction:</strong> career reorientation and upcoming decisions</li><li><strong>Conflicts:</strong> tensions within the team or with your manager</li><li><strong>Strain:</strong> dealing with pressure, stress and signs of exhaustion</li><li><strong>Parent coaching:</strong> questions about parenting, the parental role and family life</li><li><strong>Couples coaching:</strong> balancing work, family and couple time, talking through different ideas about relationships, shaping a shared vision for your private and professional future</li></ul><p>If you are unsure whether your concern is a good fit, we can clarify it in the initial contact.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">03</span><span class="rd-q">Which supervision settings do you offer?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><ul class="rd-faq-ul"><li><strong>Individual supervision</strong> for professionals in social, educational, therapeutic and medical fields as well as for people with leadership responsibilities</li><li><strong>Team supervision</strong> on collaboration, communication and role clarification within the team</li><li><strong>Group supervision</strong> for professional exchange and reflection on work with clients</li></ul><p>Whatever the setting, the focus can be on casework, leadership or team collaboration.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">04</span><span class="rd-q">How does working together begin?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>It begins with a free, no-obligation initial contact by phone or online by video. In about 20 minutes, we get to know each other and clarify the practicalities.</p><p>The first session follows. We clarify what brings you here and whether it feels right to work together. It is a regular session, charged at the usual rate.</p><p>If an organization commissions the coaching or supervision, I hold a discovery meeting with those responsible after the initial contact. There, we clarify the background, goals, scope and conditions.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">05</span><span class="rd-q">How long is a session, and how often do we meet?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><div class="faq-facts">
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Individual</span><strong>from 60 min.</strong></div>
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Two or more people</span><strong>from 90 min.</strong></div>
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Coaching</span><strong>2–4 weeks</strong></div>
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Supervision</span><strong>often monthly</strong></div>
                </div>
                <p>Individual sessions start at 60 minutes; if you wish, we can agree on longer sessions. Couples coaching and sessions with several people usually last at least 90 minutes.</p><p>Coaching usually consists of a few sessions, two to four weeks apart. Supervision often runs on an ongoing basis, for example monthly. We set the rhythm together and adjust it along the way.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">06</span><span class="rd-q">Do coaching and supervision take place on site or online?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Sessions take place in Berlin-Moabit (INSA-Berlin · Alt-Moabit 91b) or online by video. I also offer group and team supervision on site at your organization.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">07</span><span class="rd-q">Is everything we discuss kept confidential, even if my organization pays?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Yes. As a rule, what is discussed in the sessions stays confidential, even when your organization commissions the work. When we clarify the assignment, everyone involved agrees transparently on what information is passed on to management or the HR department, and in what form.</p><p>For quality assurance, I receive supervision of my own work, where I always present cases anonymously.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">08</span><span class="rd-q">What costs can I expect?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>If you pay privately, the rate is 150 euros per 60 minutes. For organizations, the fee depends on the assignment and is set out in a written offer.</p><a class="rd-faq-link" href="{{ '/en/coaching-supervision/kosten/' | url }}">All details on costs, invoicing and cancellation<span class="rd-chev"></span></a></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">09</span><span class="rd-q">What qualifications do you have in coaching and supervision?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>My work is based on recognized further training in Coaching (DGSv), Supervision (DGSv/SG) and Systemic Therapy &amp; Counseling (DGSF).</p></div></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rd-faq-detail" aria-live="polite"><div class="rd-faq-detail-bar"></div><div class="rd-faq-detail-body"></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

